|~ `::kind` and what is declared under it: the kind, its constructor, the
   verbs that build it from the noun, their refusals and their laws. The
   kind of kinds and its verbs are written as their literals, since none of
   them stands while the source runs; the chain builds every other kind.
   The rules it holds: [QSBLD#kind]. ~|

:kind
  |~~ A kind: the payload its tag is laid over, the fields it reads of the
      payload, the refusals it pages and the facts each wires, the
      invariants its values hold, its laws, and for a kind of the core its
      constructor, which its host hands. It is built from the noun by a
      chain, the commands written on it, each a verb the kind so far is the
      subject of:
      `::kind | accepts |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map | wires :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number`.
      `accepts` names the payload, its page and its kinds; `wires` a field,
      its name, its page, its selector over the payload, `/w` the key
      `w` and `~(query /h 1)` the key `h` or one, and its kinds; `tells` a
      page of the kind on a name, a chapter of a topic among them; `holds` an
      invariant of the value or of a field, its refusal, its page and its
      condition; `throws` a refusal, its page and the kind of its facts,
      the quote of its own `wires` or the tag of the refusal whose kind it
      shares; `proves` a law, its page and
      its query; and `impl ::builtin{}` the constructor of a kind of the
      core. Each command hands what it is written with to the chain, which
      holds it as it holds the literal. A value put under a kind holds the value of the kinds of its
      payload, each field read and held, and the invariants of the value,
      each refusal named under the kind, `::Box/w/KindNotTakenError`: the
      kind attaches the tag to the payload or refuses it, and builds no
      other value, but for a kind of the core, whose constructor reads its
      payload as a value of its own, `::set[2 1]` answering `#[1 2]`. A
      label is a kind declared under a name, by its chain or by its page
      alone, its verbs functions named under it: the payload, each field,
      each refusal, fact, invariant and law lie under it for `doc`, and
      `manifest` lists them but the laws, which `laws` reads; a label
      declared by its page alone holds its page and is a kind of no
      commands, which lays its tag over a payload as it is. It prints as its
      literal, its commands in a quote and its constructor or null after it,
      and reads back from it.
      ::link~(::fn | doc) ::link~(::tag | doc)
      ::link~(::qlang/verbs | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind[~(accepts
        |~~ The literal of a kind: the quote of the commands of its chain
            and its constructor, the `::builtin{}` a host hands a kind of
            the core, or null.
        ~~|
    | throws :PayloadNotPairError
        |~~ The literal of a kind is a pair, the quote of the commands of
            its chain and its constructor or null,
            `::kind[~(accepts |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map) null]`: a payload of
            another shape, a first that is no quote and a pair under
            another tag among them, is refused.
        ~~|
        ~(wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The value refused. ~~|)
    | throws :CommandNotTakenError
        |~~ Each step of the chain of a kind is a command the chain takes,
            written with the modifiers the page of its verb names in their
            order, `::kind/wires | doc` those of `wires`, whether the verb
            wrote it or the literal: `:command` holds the command as
            written, `:index` the index of the modifier refused, from zero, or
            of the first left out, and `:actualValue` the modifier.
            ::link~(::kind/accepts | doc) ::link~(::kind/wires | doc)
            ::link~(::kind/tells | doc)
            ::link~(::kind/holds | doc) ::link~(::kind/throws | doc)
            ::link~(::kind/proves | doc)
        ~~|
        ~(wires :command |~~ The command as written, a quote of its step. ~~| ::quote
          | wires :index
              |~~ The index, from zero, of the element refused. ~~|
              ::number
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The value refused. ~~| ~(query /actualValue))
    | throws :NameDeclaredTwiceError
        |~~ A name of a kind is declared once: the payload, each field,
            refusal, fact, invariant and law by its name, and an invariant
            names no refusal the kinds of its field name,
            `:w/KindNotTakenError`.
        ~~|
        ~(wires :name |~~ The name asked for, a keyword or a tag. ~~| #[::keyword ::tag]
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The value refused. ~~|)
    | throws :NameUnderNoFieldError
        |~~ A refusal or an invariant written with a path is named under a
            field read before it, `:w/NegativeError`.
        ~~|
        ~(wires :name |~~ The name asked for, a keyword or a tag. ~~| #[::keyword ::tag]
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The value refused. ~~|)
    | throws :LawUnderNoNameError
        |~~ A law written with a path is named under a name the kind
            declares before it: a field, a refusal, an invariant, a fact,
            the payload, or a refusal the kinds of the payload or of a
            field name, `proves :w/KindNotTakenError/refusesAString …`.
        ~~|
        ~(wires :name |~~ The name asked for, a keyword or a tag. ~~| #[::keyword ::tag]
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The value refused. ~~|)
    | throws :ConstructorKindNotTakenError
        |~~ The constructor of a kind is the one a host hands a kind of the
            core, `::builtin{}`, or null, whether `impl` gives it or the
            literal writes it: a kind attaches its tag by its commands, and
            code that would build another value from the payload is no
            part of it.
        ~~|
        ~(wires :expected |~~ The kinds taken, where a value of none of them was refused. ~~| ::set
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The value refused. ~~|)
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ A payload of none of the kinds `accepts` names is refused under
            the kind, `::number/PayloadKindNotTakenError`, and one that is no
            vector where it names the kinds of each element: every such
            refusal is closed by the kind of this one, the page of each
            standing under its own kind, and one a constructor raises shares
            it by its tag, `::trace/PayloadKindNotTakenError`.
            ::link~(::kind/accepts | doc)
        ~~|
        ~(wires :expected |~~ The kinds the payload takes. ~~| ::set
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the payload refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The payload refused. ~~|)
    | throws :ElementKindNotTakenError
        |~~ An element of none of the kinds named for each element of the
            payload or of a part is refused under the kind or under the
            part, `::Nums/ElementKindNotTakenError`, the first element so
            refused: every such refusal is closed by the kind of this one,
            and one a constructor raises shares it by its tag,
            `::doc/ElementKindNotTakenError`.
            ::link~(::kind/accepts | doc) ::link~(::kind/wires | doc)
        ~~|
        ~(wires :index |~~ The index, from zero, of the first element refused. ~~| ::number
          | wires :expected |~~ The kinds each element takes. ~~| ::set
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the element refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The element refused. ~~|)
    | throws :KindNotTakenError
        |~~ A part of none of the kinds its `wires` names, or one that is no
            vector where it names the kinds of each element, is refused
            under the part, `::Box/w/KindNotTakenError`: every such refusal is
            closed by the kind of this one, and one a constructor raises
            shares it by its tag, `::fn/RecipeKindNotTakenError`.
            ::link~(::kind/wires | doc)
        ~~|
        ~(wires :expected |~~ The kinds the part takes. ~~| ::set
          | wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the part refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The part refused. ~~|)
    | throws :NotGivenError
        |~~ A part its selector does not find in the payload is refused
            under the part, `::Box/w/NotGivenError`, the payload its
            `actualValue`: every such refusal is closed by the kind of this
            one.
            ::link~(::kind/wires | doc)
        ~~|
        ~(wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the payload. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The payload the part is missing from. ~~|)
    | throws :NotReadError
        |~~ A part whose selector fails on the payload is refused under the
            part, `::Box/w/NotReadError`, the error at rest of the failure
            its `actualValue`: every such refusal is closed by the kind of
            this one.
            ::link~(::kind/wires | doc)
        ~~|
        ~(wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the error, `::error` or the tag of its site. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The error at rest of the failure the selector answered. ~~|)
    | throws :InvariantNotHeldError
        |~~ A value or a part an invariant of the kind does not hold of is
            refused under the name the invariant gives,
            `::Pos/NotPositiveError`: every such refusal is closed by the
            kind of this one, and a refusal a constructor or a primitive
            raises of a value its rule does not hold of shares it by its
            tag, `::group/PayloadEmptyError`.
            ::link~(::kind/holds | doc)
        ~~|
        ~(wires :actualTag |~~ The kind of the value refused. ~~| ::tag
          | wires :actualValue |~~ The value or the part the invariant refused. ~~|)
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/readsTheKindsTaken
        |~~ A payload a kind refuses answers the kinds it takes. ~~|
        ~(::number"5" !| get [~(expected) ~(found)] | eq [#[::number] "5"])
    | proves :ElementKindNotTakenError/readsTheIndexOfTheElement
        |~~ An element of a payload a kind refuses answers its index. ~~|
        ~(::span[0 1 1 "x" 1 5] !| get [~(index) ~(found | get /3)] | eq [3 "x"])
    | proves :KindNotTakenError/readsThePartRefused
        |~~ A part of none of its kinds answers itself. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~| (::kind | wires :w |~~ The width. ~~| ::number) | ::Box{:w "x"} !| get [~(expected) ~(found)] | eq [#[::number] "x"])
    | proves :NotGivenError/readsThePayload
        |~~ A part the payload lacks answers the payload. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~| (::kind | wires :w |~~ The width. ~~| ::number) | ::Box{:h 1} !| found | eq {:h 1})
    | proves :NotReadError/readsTheFailureAtRest
        |~~ A part whose selector fails answers the failure at rest. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~| (::kind | wires :w |~~ The width. ~~| ~(get /n | add 1)) | ::Box{:n "x"} !| found | tag | eq ::number/add/SubjectNotNumberError)
    | proves :InvariantNotHeldError/readsTheValueRefused
        |~~ A value an invariant of its kind refuses answers itself. ~~|
        ~(:Pos |~~ A positive number. ~~| (::kind | holds :NotPositiveError |~~ Above zero. ~~| ~(gt 0)) | ::Pos#-3 !| found | eq -3)
    | proves :isBuiltByCommands
        |~~ A kind is built from the noun. ~~|
        ~(::kind | accepts |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map | tag | eq ::kind)
    | proves :printsAsItsLiteral
        |~~ A kind prints as its commands and its constructor. ~~|
        ~(::kind | accepts |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map | print | eq "::kind[~(accepts |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map) null]")
    | proves :listsItsNamesButItsLaws
        |~~ `manifest` lists what lies under a kind but its laws, which
            `laws` reads.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~| (::kind | wires :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number | proves :holds |~~ It holds. ~~| ~(true))
          | ::Box
          | get [~(manifest) ~(laws | keys)]
          | eq [#[::Box/w] #[:holds]])
    | proves :laysTheTagOfALabelOfItsPageAlone
        |~~ A label declared by its page alone lays its tag. ~~|
        ~(:Shop |~~ A shop. ~~| | ::Shop{:a 1} | tag | eq ::Shop)
    | proves :readsBackFromItsPrint
        |~~ The print of a kind reads back as the kind. ~~|
        ~(::kind | accepts |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map | :k it | print | parse | open | eq k)
    | proves :laysItsTagOverThePayload
        |~~ A value put under a kind is the payload under its tag. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | accepts |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map)
          | ::Box{:w 1}
          | get [~(tag) /w]
          | eq [::Box 1])
    | proves :isALabel
        |~~ A kind declared under a name is a label the scope reads. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | accepts |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map) | kinds | has ::Box)
    | proves :refusesAPayloadOfNoneOfItsKinds
        |~~ A payload of none of the kinds `accepts` names is refused under
            the kind.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | accepts |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map) | ::Box#5 !| tag | eq ::Box/PayloadKindNotTakenError)
    | proves :refusesAnElementOfNoneOfItsKinds
        |~~ Where `accepts` names the kinds of each element, an element of
            none is refused with its index.
        ~~|
        ~(:Nums |~~ Numbers. ~~| (::kind | accepts |~~ The numbers. ~~| [::number])
          | ::Nums[1 "a"]
          !| get [~(tag) ~(index)]
          |  eq [::Nums/ElementKindNotTakenError 1])
    | proves :holdsThePayloadOfItsKind
        |~~ The payload is of the kinds its `accepts` names by its own tag, a
            payload under another tag refused.
        ~~|
        ~(:Count |~~ A count. ~~| (::kind | accepts |~~ The number. ~~| ::number)
          | get [~(::Count#3 | payload) ~(::Count::Width#3 !| get [~(tag) ~(found | tag)]) ~(::Width#3 | payload | tag ::Count)]
          | eq [3 [::Count/PayloadKindNotTakenError ::Width] ::Count#3])
    | proves :readsAField
        |~~ A field of none of its kinds is refused under the field. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | wires :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number)
          | ::Box{:w "x"}
          !| tag
          |  eq ::Box/w/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :refusesAFieldLeftOut
        |~~ A field whose path the payload leaves out is refused. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | wires :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number) | ::Box{} !| tag | eq ::Box/w/NotGivenError)
    | proves :givesAFieldADefault
        |~~ A field read by `query` gives a default. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | wires :h |~~ The height. ~~| ~(query /h 1) ::number) | ::Box{} | tag | eq ::Box)
    | proves :pagesAFieldUnderIt
        |~~ The page of a field is the page of its node under the kind. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | wires :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number)
          | ::Box/w
          | doc
          | content
          | trim
          | eq "The width.")
    | proves :pagesTheRefusalOfTheKindsOfAFieldByItsField
        |~~ The refusal the kinds of a field name reads the page of the
            field where `throws` gives it no page.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | wires :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number)
          | ::Box/w/KindNotTakenError
          | doc
          | content
          | trim
          | eq "The width.")
    | proves :readsAFieldByItsNameAlone
        |~~ A field is read by its name, bare, and no path reads beneath
            the tag of its kind.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | wires :w |~~ The width. ~~| ~(get /w) ::number)
          | ::Box{:w 1}
          | get [~(w) ~(get /w !| tag)]
          | eq [1 ::path/TagClosedError])
    | proves :holdsTheInvariantsOfItsValue
        |~~ A value that breaks an invariant of the kind is refused under
            it.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | holds :TooWideError |~~ No wider than high. ~~| ~(subOf /h /w | gte 0))
          | ::Box{:w 3 :h 2}
          !| tag
          |  eq ::Box/TooWideError)
    | proves :holdsTheInvariantsOfAField
        |~~ A field that breaks an invariant written under it is refused
            under the field.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | wires :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number | holds :w/NegativeError |~~ No width below zero. ~~| ~(gte 0))
          | ::Box{:w -1}
          !| tag
          |  eq ::Box/w/NegativeError)
    | proves :PayloadNotPairError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no pair. ~~|
        ~(::kind[1] !| tag | eq ::kind/PayloadNotPairError)
    | proves :PayloadNotPairError/refusesCommandsThatAreNoQuote
        |~~ The commands of a chain are a quote. ~~|
        ~(::kind[[] null] !| tag | eq ::kind/PayloadNotPairError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesACommandItsVerbWrites
        |~~ A command its verb writes with what the chain does not take is
            refused as the literal's is, the command its `:actualValue`.
        ~~|
        ~(::kind | wires 5 |~~ x ~~| /x !| get [~(tag) ~(command) ~(index) ~(actualValue)] | eq [::kind/CommandNotTakenError ~(wires 5 |~~ x ~~| /x) 0 5])
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesAStepThatIsNoCommand
        |~~ A step of a recipe is no command of a kind. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(add 1) null] !| tag | eq ::kind/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesACommandOfAFunction
        |~~ A command of a function is no command of a kind. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0) null] !| tag | eq ::kind/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesAFieldNamedWithAPath
        |~~ The name of a field is one segment. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(wires :w/x |~~ A w. ~~| /w) null] !| tag | eq ::kind/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesThePayloadAsAField
        |~~ The payload is no field. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(wires :payload |~~ A payload. ~~| /p) null] !| tag | eq ::kind/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesASelectorThatIsNoPathOrQuote
        |~~ A selector is a path or a quote. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(wires :w |~~ A w. ~~| 0) null] !| tag | eq ::kind/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesAWordOfALiteralAsAField
        |~~ A word of a literal is no field, which the chain refuses. ~~|
        ~(::kind | wires :null |~~ Nothing. ~~| /n !| tag | eq ::kind/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :CommandNotTakenError/refusesAnEmptySetOfKindsOfEachElement
        |~~ The kinds of each element are one kind at least, a vector of the
            set of none refused by the chain.
        ~~|
        ~(::kind | accepts |~~ w ~~| [#[]] !| tag | eq ::kind/CommandNotTakenError)
    | proves :NameDeclaredTwiceError/refusesTwoFieldsOfOneName
        |~~ Two fields of one name are refused. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(wires :w |~~ A w. ~~| /w | wires :w |~~ Again. ~~| /x) null] !| tag | eq ::kind/NameDeclaredTwiceError)
    | proves :NameDeclaredTwiceError/refusesAnInvariantNamedAsTheRefusalOfKinds
        |~~ An invariant named as the refusal of its field's kinds is
            refused.
        ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(wires :w |~~ A w. ~~| /w ::number | holds :w/KindNotTakenError |~~ Positive. ~~| ~(gt 0)) null] !| tag | eq ::kind/NameDeclaredTwiceError)
    | proves :NameUnderNoFieldError/refusesARefusalUnderNoField
        |~~ A refusal under a name no field reads is refused. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(throws :x/TooBigError |~~ Too big. ~~|) null] !| tag | eq ::kind/NameUnderNoFieldError)
    | proves :LawUnderNoNameError/refusesALawUnderNoName
        |~~ A law under a name the kind does not declare is refused. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(proves :x/holds |~~ An x. ~~| ~(true)) null] !| tag | eq ::kind/LawUnderNoNameError)
    | proves :ConstructorKindNotTakenError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no constructor of a host. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~() 5] !| get [~(tag) ~(expected)] | eq [::kind/ConstructorKindNotTakenError #[::builtin ::null]])
    | proves :ConstructorKindNotTakenError/refusesCode
        |~~ Code that would build another value is refused. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~() ~(add 1)] !| tag | eq ::kind/ConstructorKindNotTakenError))
    ::builtin{}]

:kind/accepts
  |~~ Names the payload of a kind, its page and its kinds,
      `::kind | accepts |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map`: a payload whose own tag
      names none of them is refused under the kind, a payload under another
      tag among them, and an `accepts` that writes no kinds takes any payload;
      a vector of kinds names the kinds of each element, each read through
      its tags, and a payload that is no vector is refused. A set of no
      kinds, `#[]`, takes no payload, as a tag that names verbs or pages
      alone writes it, `::tagged`.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on |~~ The noun itself, which starts the kind, or a kind. ~~| ::tag
    | takes :modifiers
        |~~ The modifiers of the command as written: the page of the payload, a
            doc, and its kinds, a tag or a set of tags, the set of none taking
            no payload, or a vector of one tag or set of one tag or more for
            the kinds of each element, any value where none is written.
        ~~|
        ~(it)
    | returns |~~ The kind with its payload. ~~| ::kind
    | throws :SubjectNotKindError
        |~~ `accepts` names the payload of the noun's kind,
            `::kind | accepts …`, or of a kind.
        ~~|
    | proves :pagesThePayload
        |~~ The page of the payload is the page of its node under the
            kind.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | accepts |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map)
          | ::Box/payload
          | doc
          | content
          | trim
          | eq "The sizes.")
    | proves :takesNoPayloadOfASetOfNoKinds
        |~~ A set of no kinds takes no payload. ~~|
        ~(:Topic |~~ A topic. ~~| (::kind | accepts |~~ None. ~~| #[])
          | 5 | tag ::Topic
          !| get [~(tag) ~(expected)]
          |  eq [::Topic/PayloadKindNotTakenError #[]])
    | proves :SubjectNotKindError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | accepts |~~ A number. ~~| !| tag | eq ::kind/accepts/SubjectNotKindError))
    ::builtin{}]

:kind/wires
  |~~ Wires a part of the payload of a kind to a name: its name, its page,
      its selector over the payload and the kinds it holds where they are
      given, `::kind | wires :took |~~ The seconds. ~~| /2 ::number`. The
      selector is a path into the payload, `/2` its third element, or a
      quote that decodes the part, `~(split "|" | get /1 | toNumber)`. The
      door reads each part as a value is built: a part the payload leaves
      out is refused under its name as not given, one its selector fails to
      read as not read, and one of none of its kinds as of another kind. A
      kind that wires a part closes its tag: a value of it is read by the
      names it wires alone, each bare, `card | took`, and no path reads
      or writes beneath its tag; a word of the kind sees them in its
      recipe, `~(took | div 60)`, the walk of a name stops at the tag, and
      `payload` answers the payload bare.
      ::link~(::path/TagClosedError | doc) ::link~(::any/payload | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on |~~ The noun itself, which starts the kind, or a kind. ~~| ::tag
    | takes :modifiers
        |~~ The modifiers of the command as written: the name of the field, a
            keyword of one segment, neither `payload` nor a word
            of a literal; its page, a doc; its selector over the payload, a
            path or a quote; and its kinds, as `accepts` writes them, any value
            where none is written.
        ~~|
        ~(it)
    | returns |~~ The kind with the field after the ones it read. ~~| ::kind
    | throws :SubjectNotKindError
        |~~ `wires` builds from the noun, `::kind | wires …`, or a kind. ~~|
    | proves :holdsTheKindsOfEachElement
        |~~ A field of the kinds of each element refuses an element of
            none with its index.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | wires :xs |~~ Values. ~~| /xs [::number])
          | ::Box{:xs [1 "a"]}
          !| get [~(tag) ~(index)]
          |  eq [::Box/xs/ElementKindNotTakenError 1])
    | proves :readsAPartByItsName
        |~~ A part of a value of the kind is read by the name it wires,
            bare, and a path beneath the tag is refused, repaired by the
            name.
        ~~|
        ~(:Card |~~ A card. ~~| (::kind | accepts |~~ The parts. ~~| ::vec | wires :took |~~ The seconds. ~~| /1 ::number)
          | ::Card["a" 312]
          | get [~(took) ~(get /took !| repair) ~(get /1 !| tag)]
          | eq [312 ~(took) ::path/TagClosedError])
    | proves :showsTheNamesToTheRecipesOfTheKind
        |~~ A word of the kind sees the parts of its subject by name. ~~|
        ~(:Card |~~ A card. ~~| (::kind | accepts |~~ The parts. ~~| ::vec | wires :took |~~ The seconds. ~~| /1 ::number)
          | :Card/minutes ~(took | div 60 | floor)
          | ::Card["a" 312]
          | minutes
          | eq 5)
    | proves :readsAPathAtDepth
        |~~ A path reads a field at depth. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | wires :w |~~ The width. ~~| /size/w ::number)
          | ::Box{:size {:w "x"}}
          !| tag
          |  eq ::Box/w/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :SubjectNotKindError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | wires :w |~~ A w. ~~| /w !| tag | eq ::kind/wires/SubjectNotKindError))
    ::builtin{}]

:kind/tells
  |~~ Tells a page of a kind on a name, and the kinds it tells of where
      they are given, `::kind | tells :values |~~ Values. … ~~| #[::tag ::vec]`:
      a chapter of a topic, or a page a kind keeps beside its refusals,
      laid under the kind for `doc` and `manifest`, and a law written
      under its name lies under it.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on |~~ The noun itself, which starts the kind, or a kind. ~~| ::tag
    | takes :modifiers
        |~~ The modifiers of the command as written: the name of the page, a
            keyword of one segment, neither `payload` nor a word
            of a literal; the page told, a doc; and the kinds it tells of, a tag
            or a set of one tag or more, none where none is written.
        ~~|
        ~(it)
    | returns |~~ The kind with the page. ~~| ::kind
    | throws :SubjectNotKindError
        |~~ `tells` writes a page of the noun's kind, `::kind | tells …`,
            or of a kind.
        ~~|
    | proves :laysThePageUnderTheKind
        |~~ A page told lies under the kind, the kinds it tells of its
            value.
        ~~|
        ~(:Guide |~~ A guide. ~~| (::kind | tells :start |~~ Where to start. ~~| #[::vec])
          | get [~(::Guide/start | doc | content | trim) ~(::Guide/start | binding | value)]
          | eq ["Where to start." #[::vec]])
    | proves :holdsTheLawsUnderItsName
        |~~ A law written under the name of a page lies under it. ~~|
        ~(:Guide |~~ A guide. ~~| (::kind | tells :start |~~ Where to start. ~~| | proves :start/holds |~~ It holds. ~~| ~(true))
          | ::Guide/start
          | runLaws
          | map /ok
          | eq [true])
    | proves :SubjectNotKindError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | tells :x |~~ An x. ~~| !| tag | eq ::kind/tells/SubjectNotKindError))
    ::builtin{}]

:kind/reveals
  |~~ Reveals a view of the values of a kind, `::kind | reveals :count`:
      the name of a verb of the kind that takes no value, whose answer is a
      fact of the value by that name. A host shows the views of a fact past
      the room of a fact beside the cell it keeps the fact in, each under
      the name of the fact and its own, `:actualValue/count 3410`, and the
      legend of the tag name lays them out beside the names the kind wires.
      A value shows the views of the first kind of the walk of its tags that
      reveals any, so a set shows the views of vectors.
      ::link~(::kind/wires | doc) ::link~(::cell | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on |~~ The noun itself, which starts the kind, or a kind. ~~| ::tag
    | takes :modifiers
        |~~ The modifiers of the command as written: the name of the verb
            the view reads, a keyword of one segment, neither `payload` nor
            a word of a literal.
        ~~|
        ~(it)
    | returns |~~ The kind with the view. ~~| ::kind
    | throws :SubjectNotKindError
        |~~ `reveals` names a view of the noun's kind, `::kind | reveals …`,
            or of a kind.
        ~~|
    | proves :laysTheViewInTheLegendOfItsTag
        |~~ The legend of the tag name lays a view out beside the names the
            kind wires, the kind of what its verb answers and its gloss.
        ~~|
        ~(:Bag |~~ A bag. ~~| (::kind | accepts |~~ The things. ~~| ::vec | reveals :size)
          | :Bag/size (::fn | returns |~~ How many things: it holds. ~~| ::number | impl ~(count))
          | ::Bag | legend | print | lines | last
          | eq "|~ size ::number · How many things ~|")
    | proves :SubjectNotKindError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | reveals :x !| tag | eq ::kind/reveals/SubjectNotKindError))
    ::builtin{}]

:kind/holds
  |~~ Writes an invariant of a kind, a quote under `::invariant`: the
      refusal of a value that breaks it, its page, and the condition the
      payload beneath the tag answers true to,
      `| holds :TooWideError |~~ No wider than high. ~~| ~(subOf /h /w | gte 0)`;
      written with a path it holds of a field, `:w/NegativeError`, the
      value the payload gives the field.
      ::link~(::invariant | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on |~~ The noun itself, which starts the kind, or a kind. ~~| ::tag
    | takes :modifiers
        |~~ The modifiers of the command as written: the name of the refusal of
            a value that breaks it, a keyword read as a tag, under a field read
            before it where it is written with a path; its page, a doc; and the
            condition the value answers true to, a quote.
        ~~|
        ~(it)
    | returns |~~ The kind with the invariant. ~~| ::kind
    | throws :SubjectNotKindError
        |~~ `holds` writes an invariant of the noun's kind,
            `::kind | holds …`, or of a kind.
        ~~|
    | proves :passesAValueThatKeepsIt
        |~~ A value that keeps every invariant goes under the kind. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | holds :TooWideError |~~ No wider than high. ~~| ~(subOf /h /w | gte 0))
          | ::Box{:w 1 :h 2}
          | tag
          | eq ::Box)
    | proves :SubjectNotKindError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | kind/holds :E |~~ An e. ~~| ~(true) !| tag | eq ::kind/holds/SubjectNotKindError))
    ::builtin{}]

:kind/throws
  |~~ Names a refusal of a kind, its page and the kind of its facts,
      `::kind | throws :TooWideError |~~ A parcel past its height. ~~| ~(wires :h |~~ The height. ~~| ::number)`,
      under a field where it is written with a path, the page of the
      refusal the kinds of a field name among them; a refusal a primitive
      of the kind raises is paged so. The facts are the commands of the
      kind of the refusal, a quote, which `throws` builds into the kind as
      `::fn/throws` does, the refusal of a payload and of a part a rule
      lays taking the kind of its family, `::kind/KindNotTakenError`, and
      one that shares the kind of another naming it by its tag, as
      `::fn/throws` does.
      ::link~(::fn/throws | doc) ::link~(::kind/KindNotTakenError | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on |~~ The noun itself, which starts the kind, or a kind. ~~| ::tag
    | takes :modifiers
        |~~ The modifiers of the command as written: the name of the refusal, a
            keyword read as a tag, under a field read before it where it is
            written with a path; its page, a doc; and the kind of its facts, a
            quote of `wires` or the tag of the refusal whose kind it shares,
            none where it holds its trace alone.
        ~~|
        ~(it)
    | returns |~~ The kind with the refusal. ~~| ::kind
    | throws :SubjectNotKindError
        |~~ `throws` names a refusal of the noun's kind,
            `::kind | throws …`, or of a kind.
        ~~|
    | proves :pagesTheRefusalOfKinds
        |~~ A refusal the kinds of a field name takes the page `throws`
            gives it.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | wires :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number | throws :w/KindNotTakenError |~~ The width is a number. ~~|)
          | ::Box/w/KindNotTakenError
          | doc
          | content
          | trim
          | eq "The width is a number.")
    | proves :readsTheFactsOfARefusalByTheirNames
        |~~ The error at rest of a refusal answers the facts its kind wires
            by their names.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | throws :TooWideError |~~ Too wide. ~~| ~(wires :w |~~ The width. ~~| ::number))
          | ::Box/TooWideError!{:w 9} | get [~(w) ~(trace)] | eq [9 null])
    | proves :SubjectNotKindError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | kind/throws :E |~~ An e. ~~| !| tag | eq ::kind/throws/SubjectNotKindError))
    ::builtin{}]

:kind/proves
  |~~ Writes a law of a kind, a quote under `::law`, the claim its name
      makes, its page and the query that proves it,
      `| proves :holdsItsSizes |~~ … ~~| ~(…)`, which `laws` and `runLaws`
      read under the kind; a name written with a path lays it under a name
      the kind declares before it.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on |~~ The noun itself, which starts the kind, or a kind. ~~| ::tag
    | takes :modifiers
        |~~ The modifiers of the command as written: the name of the law, a
            keyword read as a tag, under a name declared before it where it is
            written with a path; its page, the claim it proves, a doc; and the
            query that proves the claim, answering `true`, a quote.
        ~~|
        ~(it)
    | returns |~~ The kind with the law. ~~| ::kind
    | throws :SubjectNotKindError
        |~~ `proves` writes a law of the noun's kind, `::kind | proves …`,
            or of a kind.
        ~~|
    | proves :declaresALawOfTheKind
        |~~ A law of a kind runs under it. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | proves :holds |~~ It holds. ~~| ~(true))
          | ::Box
          | runLaws
          | map /ok
          | eq [true])
    | proves :SubjectNotKindError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | kind/proves :x |~~ An x. ~~| ~(true) !| tag | eq ::kind/proves/SubjectNotKindError))
    ::builtin{}]

:kind/impl
  |~~ Gives a kind its constructor, `| impl ::builtin{}`, the second part
      of the literal of the kind, `::number | binding | value | get /1`:
      the one a host hands with a kind of the core attaches the tag to a
      payload or refuses it, and one no host handed with the kind
      constructs nothing, a kind of yours laying its tag by its commands;
      code that would build another value from the payload is refused.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on |~~ The noun itself, which starts the kind, or a kind. ~~| ::tag
    | takes :constructor
        |~~ The constructor, a primitive of the host, `::builtin{}`, or
            null.
        ~~|
        /0
    | returns |~~ The kind with its constructor. ~~| ::kind
    | throws :SubjectNotKindError
        |~~ `impl` gives the constructor of the noun's kind,
            `::kind | impl …`, or of a kind.
        ~~|
    | proves :standsAsTheSecondPartOfTheKind
        |~~ The constructor stands as the second part of the literal of the
            kind.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | impl ::builtin{}) | ::Box | binding | value | get /1 | eq ::builtin{})
    | proves :refusesAConstructorThatIsNoBuiltin
        |~~ A constructor that is no `::builtin{}` is refused as the
            literal refuses it.
        ~~|
        ~(get [~(::kind | impl 5 !| tag) ~(::kind | impl ~(add 1) !| tag)] | eq [::kind/ConstructorKindNotTakenError ::kind/ConstructorKindNotTakenError])
    | proves :constructsNothingByAConstructorOfAnotherKind
        |~~ A constructor a host handed with another kind constructs
            nothing under this one.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | impl (::number | binding | value | get /1)) | ::Box"x" | tag | eq ::Box)
    | proves :SubjectNotKindError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | kind/impl ::builtin{} !| tag | eq ::kind/impl/SubjectNotKindError))
    ::builtin{}]
